fuxi: 0106 -- command channel over the USB link (logs already go to 5140)

0077 streams the console to the host as UDP 192.168.7.1:5140, so the log half
already existed and this adds only the missing direction: the phone could talk,
the host could not answer.

No UDP socket for this.  The receive path is the USB endpoint itself: a frame
with ethertype 0x88B5 is claimed in ud_rx_done before the ethernet stack sees
it, parsed as one text command, and answered with a frame built through the same
TX queue as any other traffic.  One file, ~90 lines, no in-kernel UDP server and
no deprecated socket KPI, and it works as soon as the link enumerates -- before
IP, before ARP.

Commands: help | stat | cpu | echo <text>
  stat  ue0 state, rx/tx frame counts, event count
  cpu   current core and measured clock (PMCCNTR, from 0105)

Nothing in this path prints: printf would feed the 5140 stream back into itself.

fuxi_cpu_khz() (0105) loses its static linkage here so the command handler can
call it -- without that the kernel does not link ("_fuxi_cpu_khz referenced from
_ud_thread").

Host side: tools/fuxi-netlog.py listens on UDP 5140 for the console and sends
commands as 0x88B5 frames, so one tool covers both directions.

Harness: applied=105 skipped=0; patch -p1 --dry-run clean on the post-0105 tree.
